Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: HTMLparser.c
Line: 3270
Function: htmlParseCharDataInternal
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the '\r' case, the code reads in[1] without ensuring that at least two bytes are available. The only guard is `if (partial && avail < 2)`, which is bypassed when `partial` is false. If `avail == 1` (e.g., at EOF), this results in an out-of-bounds read of in[1].

